<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lennart Torstensson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1603">1603</a>–<a href="/years/1651">1651</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lennart Torstensson was a Swedish field marshal and artillery commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. Commander of the Swedish army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1641, he won the Second Battle of Breitenfeld in 1642 and the Battle of Jankau in 1645, then advanced towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> but failed to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> after a long siege. He later served as a governor-general in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lennart-torstensson.jpg" alt="Lennart Torstensson" width="320" height="537" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lennart_Torstenson,_1603-51_-_Nationalmuseum_-_40308.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
